UPDATE tarot_cards 
SET meaning_upright = 'GENERAL ARCHETYPE: The Five of Cups is the archetype of the profound psychological transition from attachment to integration—a systemic "reset" triggered by the sudden, often jarring, loss of an established emotional structure. It marks the shift from the contemplative withdrawal of the Four into the raw, unadulterated reality of grief, regret, and the conscious recognition that a significant cycle has reached its conclusion. Visually represented by a figure mourning three spilled, empty cups while ignoring two still-standing vessels, this archetype encapsulates the human tendency to fixate on the "data of loss" rather than the "data of remaining potential." Within the framework of consciousness, this is the stage where the ego is forced to confront the impermanence of its creations; it is the brutal, necessary alchemy of transforming sorrow into wisdom. This card is not merely about sadness; it is about the structural integrity of your emotional architecture when faced with the void. It serves as a diagnostic tool that reveals exactly where your identity was overly dependent on external manifestations. When the Five of Cups emerges, your system is undergoing a massive purge of outdated emotional investments. You are being asked to witness your own grief without becoming the grief itself—to acknowledge the three fallen cups as part of the essential, entropic nature of reality, while simultaneously training your awareness to register the two cups that remain standing. This is the master class in emotional resilience: the capacity to maintain a functional internal baseline even when the external structure you spent so much time constructing has been shattered. You are invited to move past the paralysis of "what was" and begin the arduous, yet transformative, work of re-allocating your psychic energy toward the components of your life that are still viable, still nourishing, and still aligned with your evolving soul-purpose. It is a profound, albeit painful, recalibration that forces the soul to expand its definition of worth beyond the artifacts of its own desire.',
meaning_reversed = 'GENERAL ARCHETYPE: In the reversed orientation, the Five of Cups serves as a high-intensity signal of "unprocessed haunting"—a state of systemic latency where the inability to fully integrate a past loss is causing a continuous, low-frequency drain on your current operational resources. The reversal indicates that you are currently trapped in the "phantom limb" phase of grief, where you are living in the projection of what has been lost rather than the reality of what is present, leading to a profound, chronic misalignment of your psychic focus. You are essentially "stuck" in a recursive loop of self-blame, "if-only" scenarios, and historical re-enactments that consume your bandwidth and prevent you from engaging with the current cycle of potential. From an analytical perspective, this is a clear sign that you have failed to "close the session" on a past emotional transaction, and as a result, your system is suffering from a massive, multi-threaded memory leak. The reversal exposes the hidden, egoic stubbornness that refuses to accept the finality of the collapse—a desperate, often subconscious attempt to keep the past "alive" through the continuous feeding of your own regret. The reversed Five of Cups is an urgent command for a total, radical emotional audit: you must stop the output of these low-vibration, regressive scripts and face the terrifying reality of the "emptiness" you have been trying to avoid. You are being asked to drop the defensive posturing of the "victim of fate" and take full responsibility for the integration of your own history. This is a call to stop the cycle of self-punishment and perform the necessary, often brutal, work of forgiveness—not for the situation, but for your own egoic attachment to a version of reality that no longer exists. You are being tasked with the uncomfortable, yet essential, work of reconciling the past with the present, ensuring that your current vehicle is finally cleared of the residual emotional debris that has been preventing you from recognizing the new growth opportunities that are currently sitting right behind you, waiting for your attention. It is a demand to move from the passive state of mourning to the active state of reconstruction, reclaiming your sovereign ability to choose where you direct your precious life force.'
WHERE id = 5;
